window.docContents[131].resolve({"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.ISA.Decode/#file-Arm64___Trusted___ISA___Decode":{"contents":"Paper › arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/ISA › Decode.leanTier 3 · arm64-semantics\n\nTier 3 · arm64-semantics used by the computational proof and symbolic proof 6 headline theorems depend on it 1,097 of 1,299 lines trusted source ↗Trusted, reviewed with the engine. The AArch64 model in arm64-semantics is Tier 3: it is reviewed in its own repository (check-trust-guards). The declarations that the headline statements use are shown for completeness.\n\nArm64.Trusted.ISA.Decode: AArch64 32-Bit Machine Instruction Decoder* Layer / Role: Arm64 Trusted Computing Base (Role::Spec, definitions only, 0 theorems).* Purpose & Key Exports:* Arm64.decode: partial decoder BitVec 32 → Option Instr mapping 32-bit little-endian A64 instruction words to the Instr AST in Arm64.Trusted.ISA.Syntax (or none for unallocated, architecturally UNDEFINED, or unmodeled encodings).* Arm64.decodeBitMasks / decodeBitMasksValid / decodeBitMasksVal: ARM's DecodeBitMasks logical-immediate bitmask decoder (N:imms:immr → Option (BitVec 64)).* Arm64.describeUnsupportedWord / describeUnsupportedAt: diagnostic classifier for unsupported 32-bit encodings.* Trust & Assumptions: Part of the TCB (Arm64/Trusted/). Validated against the untrusted instruction encoder (Arm64/Testing/Harness/Encode.lean) and against Sail (armv9.4-a) and Unicorn (UC_ARCH_ARM64) in lockstep differential testing (run-trusted-tests).* When to read: Read when adding or auditing instruction bit-patterns or architectural UNDEFINED / CONSTRAINED UNPREDICTABLE decode guards.\n\n\n\nBitmask Immediate Decoding (DecodeBitMasks)\n\ndef decodeBitMasksLevelsL41–52 ↗#Compute the levels bitmask (esize - 1, i.e. 1, 3, 7, 15, 31, or 63) from (immN, imms) by finding the highest clear bit of immN : ~~~imms. Corresponds to HighestSetBit(immN:NOT(imms)) in ARM's DecodeBitMasks pseudocode: returns 0 when len < 1 (i.e. immN = 0 and imms = 0b11111x, which is UNDEFINED).\n\ndef decodeBitMasksValidL54–62 ↗#Validity predicate for (immN, imms, immr) in A64 logical-immediate instructions:1. levels != 0 (len >= 1 in HighestSetBit(immN:NOT(imms)));2. S != levels (the all-ones element S = esize - 1 is reserved);3. (immr &&& ~~~levels) == 0 (canonical rotation immr < esize, so each encodable 64-bit bitmask has a unique (immN, imms, immr) representation).\n\ndef decodeBitMasksValL64–88 ↗#Mask construction half of ARM's DecodeBitMasks, assuming decodeBitMasksValid.Builds S + 1 consecutive ones inside an esize-bit element (esize = levels + 1), rotates that element right by R, and then replicates it across all 64 bits by the usual doubling chain (2 -> 4 -> 8 -> 16 -> 32 -> 64). The result is the WMask of the ARM pseudocode; TMask is not needed because A64 logical immediates only use WMask.The value returned for an invalid (immN, imms, immr) is unspecified; callers should go through decodeBitMasks.\n\ndef decodeBitMasksL90–97 ↗#ARM's DecodeBitMasks as a partial function: decode a logical-immediate encoding (N, imms, immr) into the 64-bit replicated bitmask it denotes, or none if the encoding is UNDEFINED. Inverse of Arm64.encodeBitMasks.\n\nLoad/Store Sub-Decoders\n\ndef mkLoadStoreInstL103–120 ↗#Construct a general-purpose single-register load/store Instr (Instr.ldr or Instr.str) from sizeBits (bits[31:30]), opc (bits[23:22]), target register rt, and addr : AddrMode.\n\ndef decodeSimdLoadStoreTypeL122–135 ↗#Decode (sizeBits, opc) for a SIMD/FP single-register load/store into (isLoad, sz, scale).\n\nMain 32-Bit Instruction Decoder (decode)\n\ndef decodeL141–1151 ↗#Decode a 32-bit little-endian AArch64 machine word into Option Instr.\n\n4 declarations not shown (lines 1153–1297): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesArm64.hexWord32, Arm64.hexAddr64.go, Arm64.hexAddr64, Arm64.describeUnsupportedWord, Arm64.describeUnsupportedAt\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/ISA/Decode.lean","id":"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.ISA.Decode/#file-Arm64___Trusted___ISA___Decode"}});